-#### Civics (AI)
-
-- Fix the issue of AIs autopicking/overvaluing the former civic_emancipation (or any civic with `iCivicPercentAnger`) just because other rivals have it regardless of how good the civic itself is (the former civic_emancipation was really weak yet still picked by AIs). Now replaced with opportunistic current unhappiness per city-based logic if it benefits us (only pick such a civic if enough of our cities that are unhappy because of the anger civic effect would gain happiness from it). Change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_civicValue`. Hopefully makes stronger civic choices thanks to this changes as appears to be so in autoplay before vs after change. See for details [KI#75](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#75---tremendously-improved-ais-autopicking-civic_emancipation-icivicpercentanger-just-because-other-rivals-have-it-regardless-of-how-good-the-civic-itself-is-now-replaced-with-opportunistic-current-unhappiness-per-city-based-logic-if-it-benefits-us-in-cvplayeraiai_civicvalue).
-- Fix the issue of AIs almost always picking civic_caste_system and then sticking to it no matter what: rewrote the unlimited specialist old logic in `CvPlayerAI::AI_civicValue` that would only value culture specialists, which seemingly led to civic_wage_labor (as of now unlimited engineers, see latest sevopedia/xml for updated values and details) never being picked, even when AIs would much benefit from it, including when our ennemies are stronger than us (no point to run a scientist and then die, better capitalize on engineers or serfdom or such). Now we value unlimited specialists' yields (food, hammer, gold) and commerce (beakers, gold, culture, espionage) hierarchically (e.g. higher value per yield for food vs hammer, higher value per yield for beakers vs culture, etc.), so that we value unlimited specialists strategically on a per yield base. Also added high need logic (higher culture value per yield if culture win rush or BFC need quite similarly to old code, and now also higher hammer value per yield for engineers if our ennemies are strong (see code for latest settings)). Results in autoplay are very good, we now switch back and forth between civic_slavery and civic_caste_system early (no longer perma caste system), and then later civic_wage_labor is much more popular among AIs. Civic_serfdom is also sometimes switched to late in the game. So the spread overall is much more even of unlimited specialist civics amongs AIs, which is fine and good as it suits their strategical needs much more. Added anarchy counting logic to devalue civics (less attractive if costly in turns, but still as attractive if no anarchy cost (traits, golden age, wonders, etc. (at least in theory i mean but check to be sure))), but it looks we still switch a bit too much still so may need some tweaking, but even as is should lead to much stronger and responsive AI hopefully, especially following future civic reworks. See for details with screenshots and such [KI#76](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#76---tremendously-improved-ais-almost-always-picking-civic_caste_system-and-then-almost-never-changing-it-no-matter-what-unlimited-specialists-logic-favoured-only-culture-as-well-and-much-needed-an-improvement-and-generalization-in-cvplayeraiai_civicvalue).
-- Reduce excessive civics change oscillation (was partially masked by civic_caste_system being almost always picked it seems based on autoplay testing, now more prevalent after our civic valuation changes that also value other civics depending on the player's strategic needs but anyways) by adding an additional percent slack new logic (and rewriting the old logic as well) in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doCivics` so that for example a new civic needs to be at least 10% higher valuated to be chosen/switched to (tunable). Note: If percent slack is set too high, it may cause AIs to switch too rarely and react more slowly, but if too low it may be inefficient especially for players that have anarchy turns on civic change—adjust to taste. Note 2: for some reason as of now in some cases bypassed by AIs entirely for some reason, to ideally investigate but for now if not always or not left as such.
-- Fix the issue of civics that give specialist extra commerce (as of now civic_representation giving beakers, gold, culture) being almost never picked during the entire game (vs for example civic_heridetary_rule), even though the extra commerce per specialist should be quite attractive and strong especially if it applies to many specialists. Tweaked the commerce calculation formula in `CvPlayerAI::AI_civicValue` so it uses stronger advciv-sas's custom commerce weights, and stronger commerce multipliers derived from the SAS weights (both being tunable). Results in autoplay in much more prevalent as of now civic_representation picks especially in the mid/late game, with still some civic_heridetary_rule and civic_universal_suffrage picks and back and forth as well so hopefully balanced and should lead to stronger AI as the yields are overall stronger and economically more efficient generally.
