-#### Diplomacy (AI)
-
-Note: most if not all of the diplomacy ai changes affect both ai vs ai behaviour as well as ai vs human behaviour (e.g. if master is human and vassal is ai or vice versa, etc.).
-
-Note 2: master-vassal(s) changes are made with the aim that they in most cases would also benefit the vassal rather than over-strenghthening their master in a way that would in most cases be bad for the vassal's winning odds. Similarly, a stronger vassal is also more likely to be more useful so this is intended to be in the interest of the master in most cases as well. Hopefully AI would be stronger thanks to these changes both for the vassal(s) and their master.
-
-- Seemingly tremendously improved multi-war threat management by adding sanity "emergency peace" pre-checks in `UWAI::Team::considerPeace` in `UWAIAgent.cpp`, so that AI makes peace if it fights too many wars or not that many but against a combined strong enough total enemy power ratio (vs ours as base). This should make AI much stronger as it did in the sample testing where at turn 150 Hatshepsut AI who was strongest leader in the game at this stage could keep its lead until turn 200 thanks to our changes and make targeted campaigns in this sample, instead of being badly dogpiled on and actually dying before turn 200 before our changes. Hopefully these are lax enough that plenty wars still happen, but the focus is on AI survivability and efficiency, not entertainment xd, see [65 - (Seemingly tremendously improved) Hatshepsut AI who was strongest player at turn 150 is fighting many wars and dies before turn 200: added "emergency peace" sanity pre-checks in UWAI::Team::considerPeace in UWAIAgent.cpp](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#65---seemingly-tremendously-improved-hatshepsut-ai-who-was-strongest-player-at-turn-150-is-fighting-many-wars-and-dies-before-turn-200-added-emergency-peace-sanity-pre-checks-in-uwaiteamconsiderpeace-in-uwaiagentcpp-anyways-etc) for details.
-- Fixed and greatly enhanced issue of AI overvaluing low effect bonuses such as pig (gives only +1 health) that it would value at same price than some higher effect bonuses such as maize (+2 health effectively (+1, then +1 from granary we almost always have)), by adding a pre-check in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal` so that as soon as our trading partner has the tech, then we assume said party also has granaries in all cities and thus would gain +2 health from maize, then price accordingly. Therefore bonuses are not valued too high too soon (until tech is unlocked, accounts for obsolte buildings too such as as of now the byzantine empire's civ-specific stable giving happiness from horse, that would be cancelled when said building is obsoleted). Does not account wonders and cathedrals to simplify (not present in enough cities to matter), and slightly accounts for temples and monasteries to simplify as well if they were to have such bonus effects. As a result of these changes, AI should undersatnd much better the value for example of its maize or wheat or grapes (from grocer if i'm not mistaken), and value it more in trade in gold per turn, while pig or cattle or such should be valued less, so it should no longer be possible to cheese it and trade suepr aggressively junk or low-value bonuses for high gpt or other bonuses as easily as was (was quite broken tbh) or such. Hopefully leads to stronger AI trading, and fairer AI vs AI trade as well so they don't throw away their nice bonuses to lower value ones even to other AIs. Some bonuses like iron as a result would also be valued less now as they don't have happiness or health from buildings from example, but hopefully its value should still be high enough, and it's maybe fine as such as there are other paths than having iron maybe at least early (else the human player may trade it too easily or something maybe (i am not sure about this change change but maybe it will work out well in overall diplomacy and allow for more startegy rather than easy trade abuse/exploit)). Note: coastal bonuses have a more moderate version of this as we assume many cities are not coastal so they would not gain the building related bonus's extra effect quite often. We count it as such even in water heavy maps (treated the same to simplify), so fish would be worth more than pig (with as of now harbor) but less than maize or wheat for example. See [66 - (Fixed and greatly enhanced) AI overvaluing bonuses that give minor effects such as pig or cattle/cow (+1 health only), etc, that AI would value the same as maize or wheat (+2 health effectively since almost all cities have a granary and very early) or grapes (from grocer) or molluscs (from harbor) for example, by adding a pre-check in CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal to value relatively more bonuses the more effects they provide from buildings if we have their required tech of these buildings, so that humans can't abuse/exploit it with aggressive trading to become super rich xd, and also in AI vs AI trading each AI gets best or more value out of the effective value of their bonuses at least more so now](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#66---fixed-and-greatly-enhanced-ai-overvaluing-bonuses-that-give-minor-effects-such-as-pig-or-cattlecow-1-health-only-etc-that-ai-would-value-the-same-as-maize-or-wheat-2-health-effectively-since-almost-all-cities-have-a-granary-and-very-early-anyways-etc-or-grapes-from-grocer-or-molluscs-from-harbor-for-example-by-adding-a-pre-check-in-cvplayeraiai_bonustradeval-to-value-relatively-more-bonuses-the-more-effects-they-provide-from-buildings-if-we-have-their-required-tech-of-these-buildings-so-that-humans-cant-abuseexploit-it-with-aggressive-trading-to-become-super-rich-xd-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-and-also-in-ai-vs-ai-trading-each-ai-gets-best-or-more-value-out-of-the-effective-value-of-their-bonuses-at-least-more-so-now-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc) for details.
-- Added AI logic in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`to value iAI Objective bonuses more and this valuing is higher the higher `iAIObjective` is.
-- Independently from this, added logic in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal` to tell AI how to relatively value some key bonuses like as of now Copper, Iron, Horse, Camel, Elephants, depending on if buyer has one and not the other and at which era ingame. For example iron is very nice at medieval era (value x2) if buyer has horse or camel but no iron (in order to build knights), but at renaissance such a combination is not valuable as there are other units instead (musketmen for example that don't require any bonus, and cannons only requiring iron as of now). Similarly, elephants bonus is valuable at ancient and classical era, but not in medieval (war elephants fall behind so it would be at most only for building (value x0.5 i.e. half value now in trading with buyer)). Or iron/copper are not so valuable at classical if we have camel or horse or elephants (vice versa more or less), but this changes at other eras. Also horse not being valuable at ancient and classical (to simplify (camels are not useful pre-classical but to simplify)) if we have camel and vice versa for example, but not same at other eras. Hopefully leads to smarter AI trading although i didn't test it too much so far if at all hehe but at glance seems bit better. Update: now does not apply anymore to trades between members of the same master-vassal(s) locus (as it is in their interest to be mutually stronger).
-- **Aggressive tech trade discounts for widely known techs:** AIs now sell technologies known by ≥1 of their rivals at **heavy discounts** (e.g. 25% of the original cost/value), recognizing that it is better to secure **some gold** immediately via a cheap sale than to hold out and risk getting **0 gold** if a rival sells it first; implemented in `CvPlayerAI::AI_dealVal`. To compensate for this higher trading efficiency, **AI research costs** (`iAIResearchPercent`) have been adjusted (reduced/increased at higher/lower difficulties). See for details [KI#83](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#83---tremendously-improved-ais-not-trading-techs-more-aggressively-and-cheaply-when-rivals-discover-them-too-and-there-is-a-risk-they-will-beat-us-to-the-sale-leaving-us-with-nothing-rather-than-little-gold-or-such-which-would-have-been-much-better).
-- Implemented preferrential master<->vassal(s) tech trading (we are heavily more willing to tech trade with our master/vassal(s)), in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. This synergises the previous devalue techs we can get from our master/vassal(s) change (see [Technologies (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#technologies-ai)) and expands on it, not just techs that overlap with what our master/vassal(s) already know. In autoplay, this seemingly leads to better tech sharing between vassal(s) and their master (a vassal was mostly way ahead in tech and now the master has more techs). Added a second parameter to `AI_contactRoll(CONTACT_TRADE_TECH` (was using a default of 1 in the header file) so that tech trading is now more dynamic and not passively based only on personality. See for details [KI#78](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#78---improved-trade-techs-preferentially-with-our-vassals-or-master-synergises-with-the-no-overlap-previous-master-vassals-tweak--add-a-second-parameter-now-ai_contactrollcontact_trade_tech-rcontactprobmult-to-have-a-more-dynamic-tech-trading-not-only-based-on-personality-according-to-chatgpt-51-and-then-corrected-by-claude-sonnet-45s-review-check-if-accurate-anyways-etc). Update: also added vassal<->vassal siblings extra tech trading chance similarly, which leads in autoplay (since Ewuare has 2 vassals at t250) to seemingly more or less identical results, which is fine as long as not clearly harmful, and this only boosts chance, not reduces trade which may be less predictable in terms of is this beneficial or harmful.
-- If not between members of the same master-vassal(s) locus, added an alternative military power based tech trade contact chance modifier in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`, so that we have a higher chance to trade with militarily weaker players to us (safer, less likely to backstab us) and a lower chance for stronger players to us (more likely to become our ennemies or to bite us back in some way). In autoplay, seemingly results in much closer game, where the runaway Ewuare is now regularly and repeatedly caught up by other rivals and vice versa when these take the lead as well, until late in the game where game ends at turn 419 vs 288 before and was close until the last few or such dozen turns. See for details [KI#80](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#80---tremendously-improved-ai-contacting-for-tech-trades-players-that-are-stronger-even-though-this-is-more-likely-to-be-detrimental).
-- Whenever we want to contact players outside of our master-vassal(s) locus for a tech trade, first check if a member of does not already have the tech, and if so do not contact outsiders (in the hope we indirectly trade more with players within our locus rather). In autoplay, this helps Ewuare win sooner seemingly due to unlocking the military tech for dragoons one of his vassal had long ago but that he didn't have in other runs at turn 300; tech pace is otherwise more or less mostly the same. Change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. See for details [KI#79](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#79---improved-before-contacting-other-players-for-tech-trades-first-check-if-we-dont-already-have-the-tech-in-our-master-vassals-locus-and-if-so-dont-contact-the-other-players).
-- When we are evaluating the value of a tech in tech trades with players outside of our master-vassal(s) locus, extra value key military techs (high `FLAVOR_MILITARY`) if we are weaker than our ennemies/rivals, as this is what we need most to survive, not extra economy techs or such; change in `CvTeamAI::AI_techTradeVal`. As of now, most key military techs are untradeable though, which is consistent with autoplay impact being currently small, but this could help or affect gameplay more if untradeable techs is removed for some or all of the key military techs.
-- When we are evaluating the value of a tech in tech trades with players outside of our master-vassal(s) locus, moderately devalue techs that outsiders want to sell us, if any member of our locus already knows this tech; change in `CvTeamAI::AI_techTradeVal`. In autoplay, this seems to lead to AI winning more decisively as they acquire more vassals.
