-- (Attemptingly fixed or addressed) AI building too many military naval units then gets invaded on land and can't defend (10+ galleons and barely any land defender) by doing changes in `CvCityAI::AI_bestUnit`. Hopefully makes AI much stronger on land relatively even if it comes at the cost of being slightly weaker on/at naval warfare, i believe most of the critical fighting spot is on land anyway, so i hope the now (although i didn't test it) naval military unit output is still enough at least to protect workboats or such, but besides that i wouldn't want it to be a handicap and mislead it if i may say in this caseto build many naval units (10+ galleons in the screenshot in the following link and barely and land defender then die easily by a land invasion). Also, as part of this fix/tentative patch, do not build extra more military naval units if city is landlocked (i.e. for example coastal but in a lake only, these units would be quite pointless) as noted by gemini ai. Also do not build extra more naval military units if war is possible, focus on land warfare rather. Hopefully AI is stronger with these (unless playing archipelago maybe xd but even then cities wouldn't be invaded at least maybe, i hope AI is much more efficient with these at least in theory as i didn't test it but i assume it would do so), and it fixes the example 148 in base advciv issue i had reported at the time, see [README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#35---attemptingly-fixed-or-addressed-ai-building-too-many-military-naval-units-then-gets-invaded-on-land-and-cant-defend-10-galleons-and-barely-any-land-defender](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#35---attemptingly-fixed-or-addressed-ai-building-too-many-military-naval-units-then-gets-invaded-on-land-and-cant-defend-10-galleons-and-barely-any-land-defender) for details with a screenshot and such.
-- (Attemptingly fixed or addressed) AI building settlers at critical time when war is likely, instead of preparing for war: very bad as the few more units with the hammer saved could make us gain or not lose the war, while the extra city makes all our empire thinner and our units split, on top of having less units overall as well, by doing changes in `CvCityAI::AI_bestUnit` as well. I hope AI is much stronger or at least not weaker in such circumstances as i had noticed happen twice in same game in base advciv in example 47, see also [README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#36---attemptingly-fixed-or-addressed-ai-building-settlers-at-critical-time-when-war-is-likely-instead-of-preparing-for-war-very-bad-as-the-few-more-units-with-the-hammer-saved-could-make-us-gain-or-not-lose-the-war-while-the-extra-city-makes-all-our-empire-thinner-and-our-units-split-on-top-of-having-less-units-overall-as-well-anyways-etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#36---attemptingly-fixed-or-addressed-ai-building-settlers-at-critical-time-when-war-is-likely-instead-of-preparing-for-war-very-bad-as-the-few-more-units-with-the-hammer-saved-could-make-us-gain-or-not-lose-the-war-while-the-extra-city-makes-all-our-empire-thinner-and-our-units-split-on-top-of-having-less-units-overall-as-well-anyways-etc) for details. See also [README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#civilian-units](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#civilian-units) for additional or related info (settler now a national unit), which may help quite a lot AI effiency on top of adding extra strategy for all players too. Note: thanks to our changes in known issue as of now 53, this can most likely be removed if desired, AI will stick to one settler at a time now if i'm not mistaken and our new code works as intended as quickly tested successfully for privateers and galleons, and no settler at war, so if you prefer disable it if you want many settlers at a time, hopefully AI will still stick to our rule of 1 at a time or now none if danger or such. But may be fine to keep it as such.
-- disabled for AIs the unreliable unitais that are unreliable (`UNITAI_COLLATERAL` to aim for less suicides and getting baited and more focused defense or offense units, `UNITAI_PILLAGE` (no time to waste running around, this unit will not be focused attacking or defending, avoid this, inefficient, although they seem to still pillage sometimes ingame), and `UNITAI_PIRATE_SEA` again not efficient and annoying, is also part of reducing naval warfare influence (see below for details), as a result we use our hammers more efficiently to have a more effective and efficient unitais. Say a swordsman will be an attacker or a defender, but not a pillager, so the stack will be stronger, and the cities more guarded, at least in theory, results seem good, as Khmer AI could pull an early rush on Medina and capture it with a strong stack.)
-- additionally, tweaked unitais, although i don't know how effective these changes will be or if i did them at the right place (as they sometimes seem to be overriden but rarely so and maybe it me not understanding or/and knowing how this works rather or additionally but in all cases), in `CvCityAI::AI_bestUnit` and `CvCityAI::AI_bestUnitAI` and `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction` functions as of now in cvcityai. It does seem though as of now to be taken quite well into acocunt, but test to be sure. This also depends on map type (less on naval maps, a lot more on land maps, hybrid in other maps, see above links in this known issue for details), but now for example if an AI enters offense mode, and the map is a land map, say pangea, continents, etc, as best as we could classify them i mean with chatgpt 5 if i may say so check if accurate and if works as intended test to be sure, AI will more or less ignore unitais that don't help it directly in war as we instructed it, so it will value a lot more `UNITAI_ATTACK` or `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY` for example, a bit of `UNITAI_RESERVE` (visible in debug mode (ctrl+z and "chipotle") by holding ctrl or alt i forgot which while hovering on a unit or unit stack), and this means its units won't wander or such and attack more decisively at least in theory, and vice versa in defense mode they'd value these less and unitais such as `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE`, `UNITAI_CITY_SPECIAL`, `UNITAI_RESERVE` etc if any more as well i mean too, for the most part. Hopefully helps the AI better execute its attacks but many things could influence it. It will not care to produce any naval or such unitais units. So it can produce say a swordsman with the attack_city or attack or even reserve unitais maybe, but naval units can't have these, and their unitais like `UNITAI_ATTACK_SEA` or such if i'm not mistaken are tremendously less valued. This avoids the issue i had in base advciv of AI having 10 galleons but barely any land defender on a pangea if i'm not mistaken, see above links for details as well. In naval maps, if detcted as such with our code, this is toned down a bit, but the general idea remains to protect our cities first and foremost, and aim for most effiicent roles, see cvcityai for details. Also, is this galleon / trireme / galley really worth the 2-3 extra axemen / swordsmen / extra worker or half settler? Probably not, and wastes turns time to build not just ressources as in yields, so we are delayed in war plans, tech etc. I believe it is more efficient to do so at least for AIs and in most cases. I didn't test code too much, but based on it semeingly having much less barbarian successful invasions, and on the theory of efficiency behind it as i explained and ideas i got and autoplay results, it seems better for the AI to go slower, even if we lose 1-2 city spots or wonders, the benefits are larger it seems. This is a summary i attempted to do of the changes and again didn't test too much so far; while i hope it helps the AI, i am not necessarily too open to feedback, so i would suggest you best share your experience regarding this on a forum, such as CFC forum, i do hope that it helps and is enjoyable to play though. I also hope these changes fix base advciv issue of AI abandonning capital city, sometimes in a way that ruins the entire game, just to attack 1 unit. I didn't test it, but i hope with these unitais that now exclude colalteral, pillage, etc, units would be more efficient in not doing so, and better guard cities, as well as be, when on offense mode, more focused on their goal, at least in theory, but many other parts of the code could interfere or i could have gotten the logic wrong somehow. It seems to be applied quite well in few autoplays i quickly glanced at skimmed through, and making AI stronger and more capable as a result but test to be sure.
-- to avoid or reduce fake/suicidal AI war declarations, reduce iPower for some units, like and in particular naval units as warfare happens mostly on land and even if AI has 10 frigates, it will not win against 2 crossbows or even warriors for example; also adjust the estimated power of some land units like warrior, animals, etc as part of rebalancing them, see also [Long_Comments/Long_Comments_XML.txt](/Long_Comments/Long_Comments_XML.txt) (search for `UnitAI notes (Units XML)`) for details
-- reduce the flavor_military (as of now from 10 to 6 for the generic barracks (no change for the zulu barracks already at 6 in base advciv at least, see xml for details)) so that hopefully more varied types or/and there is a more even building profile of the barracks among all types of AI leaders not just the strongly military ones if i am not mistaken in my understanding +/- guess, both for defense but more importantly for offense if i am not mistaken and from asking chatgpt too with web search.
-- to compensate this reduction of flavor, also make barracks more valued by AI in all circumstances , also increase `iAIWeight` so that AIs in particular don't do too premature rushes and start building units unit they have barracks ideally so that these units are upgraded units in experience ideally, by also asking chatgpt with web search and such kujira (see useful links or somewhere in readme that mentions kujira for details) example to be sure, and also by seeing what FFH2 mod does (it uses a value of 40 for example) as of now from 0 to 70 (as of now 75 for the zulu bararcks due to extra gold effect, see xml for updated values or and details), so all AI leaders (except barbarian as it just needs more units more efficient for it i think) prioritize building barracks more, hopefully not too high so that versatility and other alternative efficient or quite efficient strategies could be explored as well,, hopefully AI would plan more and execute better their rushes with stronger in experience units even if these rushes are slightly delayed as a result
-- stables buildings: similar reasoning and balance changes, as of now `iAIWeight` from 0 to 75, see xml or and docs or/and other relevant info in our mod or outside of it maybe if helps
-- rebalanced or reworked some `DefaultUnitAI`, `UnitAIs`, and `NotUnitAIs` in the XML, to make AI go for most efficient roles, despite our units being more versatile now (see Military changes in [README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#military-and-some-civilian-units-related-info-non-exhaustive-see-sevopedia-orand-xml-for-details](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#military-and-some-civilian-units-related-info-non-exhaustive-see-sevopedia-orand-xml-for-details) for related info). In short, even though as of now swordsmen can defend for all players as in for example having access to City Garrison promotions for example, they still, for AIs, will be used only and if not mostly as offensive units, as it is more efficient to do so in most cases, and the rare edge cases are not worth making AI weaker in most cases (like defending with swordsmen and attacking with longbowmen, which would cost more hammers for worse result generally).
-- adjust unitAIs of some (mostly early as of now see xml for details and docs) siege units so they don't get baited as much instead of focusing mostly on city attack or "counter" (as in staying in city but attacking the surrounding units) defense (ideally as i didn't explicitly implement it as such but i hope they don't get baited anymore at least)
-- fixed/enhanced AI promotion choices being sometimes very inefficient such as going for woodsman (useless for city combat and in most tiles) or medic (not effective combat booster, better be stronger and die or win than waste XP with this) which is most likely to be almost always bad, or conditionally most likely to be bad such as not going for city_garrison promotion when a unit has a `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE` and vice versa for attack city unitai and city raider promotion, as well as other such cases, or going for counter_archer promotion when unitai is a defensive one (archers are rarely attackers, and if they are our other promotions cna help a bit defend against them, so better go for something else for example in such cases). I made these changes in `CvUnitAI::AI_promotionValue`, to hopefully better guide which promotions are most likely to be good and tell the AI to go for these, while hopefully preserving versatility, and if we don't have a reason to change it hopefully also preserving base advciv behaviour enough. So these are hard rules that apply before any of the old code's promotion value best promotion pondering is made, and then if these rules are successfully passed only then would AI consider as it did before which promotion to choose among the remaining ones to choose from if i may say in this case. For example, if we say that for defenders retreat promotion and city raider promotion and blitzkrieg promotions are bad (be tanky not mobile is the priority), and that no always pick first promotion was chosen, then only after passing these checks will remaining promotions (e.g. combat, first strike, etc) be considered/pondered and chosen best from if no best emerged from our hard rules before that. See more detailed rules with .md tables and nuances in [/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#47---fixed--addressed--enhanced-ai-choosing-poorly-promotions-for-its-units-now-added-a-set-of-hard-rules-in-which-case-some-promotions-are-not-good-and-to-ignore-as-is-most-efificient-in-most-times-and-rarely-cases-where-some-promotions-are-best-to-always-go-first-for-eg-as-of-no-city_garrison-first-for-unitai_city_defense-city_raider-first-for-unitai_attack_city-etc-if-any-more-anyways-etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#47---fixed--addressed--enhanced-ai-choosing-poorly-promotions-for-its-units-now-added-a-set-of-hard-rules-in-which-case-some-promotions-are-not-good-and-to-ignore-as-is-most-efificient-in-most-times-and-rarely-cases-where-some-promotions-are-best-to-always-go-first-for-eg-as-of-no-city_garrison-first-for-unitai_city_defense-city_raider-first-for-unitai_attack_city-etc-if-any-more-anyways-etc). As a result of these changes, AI promotions are seemingly much saner, and i believe AI is stronger as a result, while preserving versatility more than enough i would say maybe, see link in this bullet point for details. Note: unitai and unit are different things, so the "longbowman" unit for example could have `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE` and act as a defender or `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY` and act as an enemy city attacker. Our rules would apply differently to the longbowmen depending on its unitai (e.g. as of now allowing city raider on an offensive unitai longbowmen but not on a defensive unitai longbowmen), and as of now not on its unit combat type (for the longboman example at least, as this has some exceptions such as of now recon units combat type having its own unit combat type promotion rules with/in our changesbut they are as of now an exception(s if any more) to this).
-- addressed and seemingly fixed or greatly enhanced new AI cities being imbalancedly guarded vs stronger ones, often causing early easy barbarian captures of these (e.g. capital city has 4+ units stationned but city B only has 1 unit so easily captured). With the help of chatgpt 5 and of geminia ai 2.5 pro a bit too thanks, i added code to make sure we have at least 2 defenders to our new cities. This seems almost always applied if not always, and thanks to this AI should be a bit stronger, with less early captures, even though some still happen, but our cities are better guarded and more evenly at least, with the capital having priority. Note: as of now this is disabled after turn 120 (adjusted to game speed) to save computation, as there are many units, no barbarian threats, and although new cities should still be guarded, perhaps AI can handle it well at that time then now that it has enough units or such or in case it helps with other issues by not persisting to do it. The changes have been done as of now in `CvUnitAI::AI_update`, `CvUnitAI::AI_guardCityMinDefender`, `CvCityAI::AI_minDefenders`. See for details, with screenshots as well, [49 - (Enhanced/Addressed) AI having 4+ defenders in capital city but only 1 defender in city B, that gets captured or razed by barbarians then, now almost always if not always new cities go be founded with 2+ defenders](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#49---enhancedaddressed-ai-having-4-defenders-in-capital-city-but-only-1-defender-in-city-b-that-gets-captured-or-razed-by-barbarians-then-now-almost-always-if-not-always-new-cities-go-be-founded-with-2-defenders)
-- Tremendously enhanced AI scrapping rules/conditions, by adding pre-checks to make sure we don't scrap useful units, in particular as of now always done for land military units, as well as regardless of that for absolutely all units before turn 150. This helps solve issues of AI scrapping its macemen early just after producing them, which is pointless and very bad for its strength, be it against barbarians or other rivals. As long as economy isn't bankrupt (which we don't try to prevent but didn't happen here so fine as such), even a little extra is fine and good to have. Since it didn't seem the case and all worked great, including said AI in this example now surviving and thriving (at least not dying and doing decently well, much better than before when it scrapped its units). See also handicap changes related to these in this guide as well, and see for details with screenshots and more explanations or and such[52 - (Beyond Tremendously improved) Remove AI scrapping of military land units, as way too many units are scrapped early, yet we really need them to defend against barbarians or our rivals or such](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#52---beyond-tremendously-improved-anyways-etc-remove-ai-scrapping-of-military-land-units-as-way-too-many-units-are-scrapped-early-yet-we-really-need-them-to-defend-against-barbarians-or-our-rivals-or-such-anyways-etc)
-- musketmen now have the unitai_attack_city as well so AIs should use them offensively or more so now if i'm not mistaken, with also other changes or not depending on civ-specific variations or such
-- added unitai_city_defense to grenadier and bazooka units so AIs may use them more as defensive (here in particular in cities) units
-- seemingly tremendously improved issue of AIs getting baited to attack faraway rivals, that would leave their core cities mostly defenseless, and oftentimes dying shortly after to an opportunistic rivals. Changed by adding a pre-filter reject in war risk assessment based on distance to us in `Risk::preEvaluate` in WarUtilityAspect.cpp, so that we don't attack too far away rivals (i assume by extremely increasing risk assessment for said rivals), resulting in better AI outcomes and more focused unit troops on the map (no half of the units in a faraway city anymore it seems for the most part) on land attacks, see [61 - (Seemingly Tremendously Improved) AIs getting baited to attack faraway rivals, leaving their core cities mostly defenseless, and oftentimes dying shortly after to an opportunistic rivals. Changed by adding a pre-filter reject in war risk assessment based on distance to us in Risk::preEvaluate in WarUtilityAspect.cpp](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#61---seemingly-tremendously-improved-ais-getting-baited-to-attack-faraway-rivals-leaving-their-core-cities-mostly-defenseless-but-anyways-etc-and-oftentimes-dying-shortly-after-to-an-opportunistic-rivals-changed-by-adding-a-pre-filter-reject-in-war-risk-assessment-based-on-distance-to-us-in-riskpreevaluate-in-warutilityaspectcpp) for details.
-- (Extremely better/stronger) AI now always evacuates all its as of now land units from a doomed city rather than a small part of them or/and sometimes (before the change AI was almost not evacuating at all doomed cities (2 swordsmen only would be evacuated for example in an 11 unit defending stack vs a 22+ attacking unit stack), see an example of this with details and screenshots or/and suchin [62 - (Extremely better/stronger) AI almost not evacuating at all doomed cities (2 swordsmen in an 11 unit defending stack vs a 22+ attacking unit stack), fixed by always and 100% evacuating city doomed city regardless of land unit type, in CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-evacuating-city-doomed-city-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity)), fixed by always and 100% retreat regardless of land unit type, in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`. As a side effect, it might drag games a bit longer (although i didn't test it to know for sure) and i didn't test it too much beyond this sample case where it makes a huge difference, but i think having a more competitive and not stupid but strategic ai is much better.
-- Possibly prevented and possibly fixed the weird and very inefficient back and forth of going to attack a city stack, and then going back after seeing enemy stack is too strong, which was also very risky if our stack couldn't retreat in time (to defend cities or avoid ambush/attack or other purposes maybe). I don't know if this change fixes it since the issue was solved without it (2+ autoplay turns were needed at least it seems not 1), but maybe the additional sanity check of not (going to?) attacking(attack) city if target is too strong, in `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, helps a lot but (although would need to test to be sure but seems like a very nice sanity check if not redundant with some other checks maybe). See for details [63 - (Possibly prevented and possibly fixed) Weird / very inefficient back and forth of going to attack a city stack, and then going back after seeing enemy stack is too strong. I don't know if this change fixes it since the issue was solved without it (2+ autoplay turns were needed at least it seems not 1), but maybe this change in CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove helps a lot](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but-anyways-etc).
-- tweaked and enhanced old razing logic so we that we (i.e. AI (excluding the barbarian player itself, but as for cities applies more or less to all cities even non-barbarian ones if i'm not mistaken anyways et) players) now raze cities in the early (as of now first 120 turns adjusted to game speed) game if they are not close enough to make it worth the early investment, in `CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity`. This helps not spread our military forces (which was a major issue in base advciv when it happened, often with most troops being in the new captured faraway city while core ones would be less defended, hopefully much saner and stronger razing now) and scrace economy ressources (city maintenance would be increased per city, pop is generally low in these cities plus the time to build improvements or/and culture or such there, plus the city maintenance in the city itself, etc) so that they stay focused. Indirectly, it may often lead to less fog busting so more barbarians, which is good since it's far from us so will weaken our rivals. As a result of this, AI should be much stronger in the early game, and hopefully no longer split in two making it much easier to defeat (especially if most forces are in the new city). See [64 - (Greatly enhanced) AI not razing faraway cities at captures - now we raze them if we are in the early game and they are not close enough, thanks to changes and tweaks in CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc) for details.
-- Fixed and enhanced the issue of AI overbuilding defenders in the early game. It now tries (at least in theory in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`) to replace the unit to build with an offense of versatile leaning. Typically, this means less longbowmen and more spearmen, camel archers, axemen, etc. We avoid to produce excess siege (in particular trebuchets-like units) since they are not versatile enough to be used at defense and offense especially by the AI. The focus and assumption is we'll do good enough early where power differences are still not that great and gains potentially important to make. We also as of now favour civ-specific units (e.g. an egyptian war chariot rather than a horse archer if i'm not mistaken) most times. If no good unit candidate is found, we attempt to hijack the unitai of the defensive unit (e.g. a longbowman with attack or attack_city or counter instead of city_defense). Results are very impressive!! They don't seem to always apply or entirely apply, but it does seem like most rivals have significantly less longbowmen and a more varied composition, and sometimes the difference is massive. For example in a run, hatshepsut ai went from +/- 30+ longbowmen for +/- 6 cities at turn 130 to 32 war chariots (plus camel archers for some reason etc), while some ais had often few, sometimes many longbowmen for some reason. Still, overall the seemingly more versatile compositions for all AI players, hopefully helps them better transition into an offensive middle game strategy and not be stuck with useless excess defenders. This should help boxed in players in particular, but also any AI with excess unit, after quite minimal defense needs are met (offense units can defend then as well and are more versatile, the varied composition also indirectly helps counter picks to invade us (like building spearmen vs chariots, or axes vs swords, hopefully,)). See originally changes in [53.2 - (Fixed and enhanced) Joao AI building way too many defenders (36 longbowmen at turn 130!! Almost all with UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE or similar) while being boxed in with only 3 cities, instead of making about half of these offense units or versatile ones to punish overextending thin neighbour, fixed by having an early phase "we have expectedly too few cities at this stage of the game, no need to overbuild anymore denders at this stage of the game, switch to offense or versatile UNITAI rather" and "our military composition has way too many defender UNITAIs, switch to offense or versatile UNITAIs", which seemingly fix the issue](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) and then a more refined and enhanced, as of now final version of these in [53.2.2 (Seemingly greatly enhanced) AI overproducing defenders early on, especially longbowmen but not only, replaced with an early produce more versatile units especially civ-specific ones when defended enough (at least in theory) in CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc).
-- Tremendously improved AI overbuilding trebuchets in particular but more generally siege units, especially when it is bad like being weaker (trebuchets are useless and very hammer inefficient if not strictly to attack city tiles, catapults or cannons or such are also not too versatile or/and used correctly by AI to defend for example). Used various conditions in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to try to make siege units production as minimal as possible, up to none at all if needed, but if other conditions are methopefully not too low (a bit low as of now but much better than before when it was too strong). As a result, AIs should have a more varied offensive stack composition, as well as being better at defense when weaker, as seems the case in autoplay test i ran at a glance. See for details [53.3 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding siege units, in particular trebuchets but not only, where they are detrimental to do build, in particular when weaker but not only](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc). Update: since then, relaxed siege thresholds in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and in the fallback unit if no production code as well in `CvCity::doTurn`: slightly relaxed them before renaissance, and relaxed them extra more if we have key strategic bonus (as of now iron, copper, horse, camel, elephants) as siege units may help us do a successful longbow rush or such if we fit the other offense conditions to produce them, and heavily relaxed them at renaissance+ as cannons as a viable alternative to a defender, especially if we have no mounted bonus and no access to muskets yet, overbuilding pikemen against cuirassiers is useless, ineffective, and will bankrupt us sooner. More generally also allows more varied stacks compositions and much better results ingame for some AIs it seems that had the issue of dying due to having too much pikemen and keeping to build them when cannons and later siege units are available and much stronger / more effective, but check to be sure.
-- removed `UNITAI_CITY_COUNTER` from non-versatile enough units such as the UNIT_MACEMAN, as they are not versatile enough to be reliable city defenders while still being good offense units (too easy to punish with a stack of knight units that are good against them, even a crossbow stack could defeat defending macemen, so use them for offense rather and disable them from here as well as in similar places). They may be good against pikemen, but pikemen don't often attack cities and are not that efficient for that, so prefer macemen to focus more on offense unitai roles, and same for other units if any have that issue as well.
-- removed `UNITAI_COUNTER` from mounted units that had it (UNIT_CHARIOT, UNIT_EGYPTIAN_WAR_CHARIOT, UNIT_CARTHAGE_NUMIDIAN_CAVALRY) as they are not strong enough defender units to warrant it (doesn't ""receive defense bonuses" (i.e. modifiers), plus takes a longbowman slot inefficiently as well i mean), and are wasted as a non attacker (stays parked in cities sometimes for example for the egyptian war chariot if i remember it correctly). For chariot class units in particular, it may have made sense when longbows were available much later, but now in our modthey are available at about same time in tech as axeman class units, and are a more versatile, cheap enough and overall stronger defender, so prefer it for that purpose rather and use chariots offensively if in window to do so else don't build them (rather than park them in cities).
-- Tremendously improved AI overbuilding very cheap (as of now 20 or less hammer cost in unitinfo XML (indepent from any trainpercent modifier)) combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient, nonsensical since there are so many better options like swordsmen, chariots, longbowmen, anything else basically some of which not requiring any bonus, and easy to overshoot, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless. Since they are easy to overbuild due to being so cheap, they may quickly make us bankrupt, and are not so effective per unit. As in our mod archers are as of now available very soon, fairly cheap, and more versatile and overall stronger, plus since they also help fill our defense needs/quotas sooner so we move to offense focus sooner, it seems very nice to be able to cut down on excess very cheap units, as of now only the ancient maceman (note: this trims down scouts as well since they have combat, but we don't seem to overproduce them so fine, and even if we were to then would be handled by the same cap). As a result of these changes in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, ingame, we seem to have much better compositions (e.g. 3 ancient macemen at turn 100-130 vs 11 before in AI players), and much more stronger units in comparison. Hopefully helps being economically efficient as well. AI should be stronger as a result of these changes hopefully. See for details [53.4 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding very cheap combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient and easy to overshoot, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless; much better military compositions and better growth as a result](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#534-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-very-cheap-combat-units-ancient-macemen-only-being-an-issue-as-of-now-anyways-etc-in-the-early-game-sometimes-even-at-turn-100-which-is-inefficient-and-easy-to-overshoot-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-as-they-are-cheap-and-accumulate-quickly-but-are-not-too-effective-especially-as-soon-as-we-get-archer-units-anyways-etc-now-limited-especially-even-more-so-after-as-of-now-turn-50-where-they-should-be-especially-useless-much-better-military-compositions-and-better-growth-as-a-result-anyways-etc). Update: now the anti excess very cheap units is also included in `CvCity::doTurn` in the no production fallback unit code, as we were producing too many fallback ancient macemen otherwise with the new offense only code (like 19 ancient macemen at turn 100 which is very inefficient and most likely to bankrupt us or ruin our game). Update 2: Also added renaissance plus (anti pikemen or such, but only for land AND direct combat units (no scouts, spies, etc.)) logic as well as these units are ineffective against gun and higher units, and economically very inefficient (high spam and unit cost, low combat potential vs lower unit costs for stronger units or/and possibly more buildings as well).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5286+) **AI stack attack order — spend expendables first:** AI stack attacks now prefer **bombard/collateral** and **low-effective-strength/low-XP** units first (once the stack commits to attack), preserving elite finishers. Rationale: economically efficient (older/weaker units cost upkeep but scale poorly) and strategically safer (keep high-value units for decisive blows or retreats). Change in `CvSelectionGroupAI::AI_getBestGroupAttacker`. Toggle via SAS defines for A/B testing. See [KI#89](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#89---improved-in-an-attack-stack-attack-with-lower-value-effective-strength-xp-health-units-first).
-- AI now favours a military instructor specialist rather than a great general leader, as this is much stronger and scales better with late game. Added logic to favour top hammer city decrementially (top 1 hammer city the most, then top 2 city a bit less but still a lot, etc.), and tweaked existing logic to favour top as of now 3 hammer cities tremendously more. Also added logic to favour city especially more if it has or is building the heroic epic effect building (or whichever equivalent is in your mod mod if you modified it and implemented it as such in sas defines as well). Also, removed the military instructor per city limit, so now an AI city can have many military instructors not 1 max, which is much stronger. Changes in `CvCityAI::AI_permanentSpecialistValue` and `CvUnitAI::AI_generalMove`. See [KI#69](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#69---tremendously-improved-ai-going-for-great-general-leaders-while-military-instructors-are-much-better-with-added-logic-to-favour-top-hammer-cities-remove-military-instructor-per-city-limit-favour-it-further-if-have-or-building-heroic-epic-effect-building-etc) for details. Note: sometimes it seems to rarely be ignored in autoplay for some reason, although mostly applied it seems.
-- **Unit upgrades - stop wasting gold on tiny gains:** Fix AI tendency to **over-upgrade units** even when the upgrade is **poor value** (high gold cost for a small strength gain), which can burn many turns of **gold** and **slow tech pace**. Before allowing an upgrade, the AI must pass **simple ROI gates** based on **strength** gained vs gold cost: (1) gold per 10% strength gain, and (2) gold per +1 **flat strength** gain; both gates are **more lenient with higher unit EXP** (high-EXP units keep their promotions after being upgraded which is valuable, so spending more gold on them is more justified), while low-EXP units are treated more strictly (often better to let them die and rebuild if needed, unless it is cheap enough to upgrade them). Example (Knight -> Cuirassier): 10 strength -> 13 strength; if one of the gates requires `15 gold per +1 flat strength gain` with `+1 gold per +1 flat strength gain per 1 EXP`, then we won't upgrade the unit if its upgrade cost is more than `15 * 3 = 45 gold` at **0 EXP**, or `((15 + 18) * 3) = 99 gold` at **18 EXP** for this gate. In autoplay, this seemingly leads to **all AIs teching significantly faster**, especially in the **late game** where there are many units and AI would often have its tech pace stall for dozens of turns. Change in `CvUnit::canUpgrade` (single global gate, like `CvUnit::canScrap`); see [KI#88](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#88---tremendously-improved-ai-always-upgrading-way-too-much-units-and-not-teching-at-all-sometimes-for-dozen-turns).
