-### Military and some civilian units related info (non-exhaustive, see sevopedia or/and xml for details)
-
-- new camel units (as of now Camel Archer, Camel Knight, Camel Cuirassier) related to the BONUS_CAMEL changes, as an alternative to horse units. Also reworked the arabian empire's civ-specific unit so as the Hajjan, a Camel Knight variant.
-- Unit combat types refers to unit categories/types, for example in Civ4 BTS/base AdvCiv these were for example archery units, recon units (scout, explorer, (now also added the airship, see below)), melee units (spearman, axeman, swordsman, maceman, pikeman, etc.), etc. There are many new unit combat types, still a todo as of now but some have been implemented already (not sure will be done further or/and immediately nor soon if at all, may or may not), see the sevopedia entry "Unit Combat Types" for details. This allows to give specific bonuses to specific combat types. For example, there are now new combat types of units (and modified existing ones too), for example the archers combat type is now subdivided instead into new archers (bow, short), archers (long), and archers (crossbow) if one wants to give specific combat modifiers based on these types more specifically (i.e. modifier vs crossbows but not vs longbowmen, or vs short bows and longbows but not vs crossbows or a different modifier); as of now if i am not mistaken though there should not be much if at all differences between how these units are handled so this is as of now only a functional difference if i may say but ideally one may want to add differences between them maybe, for example crossbows defending first or such against units, but not implemented in advciv-sas as of now if i am not mistaken (didn't check but i don't remember such a change or type of change).
-- in particular, split unitcombat_melee units into unitcombat_melee_polearm (i.e. using a lance (melee but from some distance), e.g. spearman, pikeman, etc if any more) and unitcombat_melee_shock (i.e. close range / contact / brawl, e.g. ancient maceman, axeman, swordsman, maceman, etc if any more). For example, after this change, axemen now are still good against polearm units (they crush spears xd) but they are now barely stronger than swords (just a bit as of now); also, crossbows are still strong vs medieval macemen (unitcombat_melee_shock) but now useless vs pikes (unitcombat_melee_polearm). This fixes the issue of bronze units like the axeman being stronger than medieval pikes which was non-sensical considering the age and cost difference, or if not this one of any unit we'd want to add or rework. Also, some civ-specific variants like as of now the persia_immortal (swordsman variant) are now correctly typed as melee_polearm since they are holding a lance, which means their modifier vs melee_shock makes them bit stronger than other swords (which makes sense since they have a lance and fight from a distance vs them), while their overall kit remains good enough to withstand well enough axes as we intend too. Also allows for more fine tuning for example with the as of now babylonian bowman, or the generic crossbow, now being strong specifically against melee_shock and not vs melee_polearm (in other words crossbows and such are useless against pikes (since they are armor as in heavy defensive generally units or/and use a metaphorical or real shield) as we intend). General idea for mounted units: Spearman > Chariot (UNITCOMBAT_MOUNTED_MELEE); generic Horse/Camel Archer (UNITCOMBAT_MOUNTED_RANGED) > Spearman; generic Horse/Camel Knights (UNITCOMBAT_MOUNTED_MELEE) < Pikemen (UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_POLEARM); generic Horse/Camel Cuirassiers > Pikemen (UNITCOMBAT_MELEE_POLEARM). See sevopedia or/and xml for details.
-- some units are now in another combat type, for example as of now the mechanized_infantry is now in armored units, not in gun units anymore.
-- This also changes warfare tactics and such for some other unit combat where i made such small or not modifications in this case, for example mounted units are now split into mounted melee and mounted range units, so for example pikemen as of now are strong against mounted melee (like the horse knight) but not against the mounted ranged (such as the horse archer or cuirassier for example). Also note that some civ-specific units are not in same combat type than their generic "parent" if i may say, for example the ballista elephant is mounted ranged vs the war elephant being mounted melee if i may say. I have tweaked a bit the advantages of most of the mounted melee units to buff them relatively a bit as they would be a bit weaker otherwiseas of now at least, also there are other small or not differences such as the defend order or such too if i am not mistaken. Also for example the anti tank infantry and the gunship would now be strong against mechanized infantry if i am not mistaken for example too as of now at least it would be so. The airship is now a recon unit, not an air unit anymore, meant to be a defensive more effective recon unit than the explorer (also note: the airship as of now cannot see submarines anymore unlike later recon unit(s), see sevopedia unit chart and sevopedia unit of the corresponding units for details), see sevopedia unit for updated values.
-- All units now are affected by city defenses (walls, castles, etc if any more/other), even gunpowder and later on units, seems more realistic to me this way, as walls can help against guns and against all (almost?) units, actually even if not having the tech for guns itself. See also for details: bIgnoreBuildingDefense in CIV4UnitInfos.xml or/and (tranlslate to english ((following) web page) using web browser or such) [https://gforestshade.github.io/kujira/post/civ4unitinfos/#bignorebuildingdefense](https://gforestshade.github.io/kujira/post/civ4unitinfos/#bignorebuildingdefense) for details (too(.))
-- fixed the stealth bomber and other units having a lower collateral damage limit than its base collateral damage (`<iCollateralDamage>100</iCollateralDamage>` vs `<iCollateralDamageLimit>50</iCollateralDamageLimit>`), which i don't know a lot about but seems like a mistake or inconsistent with most units (why put a higher than the limit damage, again i could be mistaken about how this works-functions, but we (i.e. mexd...) also wanted to add more collateral damage support so now all units have some (swordsmen could throw shurikens) collateral damage limit, even though collateral damage itself starts at 0 for most units still; such info is now displayed in sevopedia unit chart (as of now named "Combat" category, as well as in each unit's sevopedia unit placeSpecial (as of now named "Special Abilities" panel)), and also ingame in map view when hovering over the unit, in its effects panel (we also now show more reliably the extra collateral damage info there as well); also as a result and in line/following this change, as of now collateral damage 1 and 2 promotions are available to all eligible units (which should be all or almost all, see sevopedia promotion or sevopedia unit for details); hopefully i am not mistaken in doing so or/and it is helpful or not or yes or etc)
-- unit promotions are reworked or/and rebalanced: woodsman for example is buffed, some other like Hills Master 2 and 3 (guerilla) are rebalanced or nerfed, and other some promotions have also their requirements changed, for example archers have access to city bombard promotion (units are reworked too, see below), or "Logistics" (named "Commando" before) is now accessible after Combat 1 or City Raider 1, or City Raider 3 or City Garrison 3 or First Strike 3 as of now also require (i.e. additionally, on top of previous prereq) Combat 2 before that not only the previous level (else was a bit too op before i think). Some are available sooner too, for example "Logistics" is available at "The Wheel", not "Military Science" anymore, since we understand roads we can use them, maybe, more strategic importance now too maybe hopefully.
-- removed some promotions such as PROMOTION_TACTICS, as effect is redundant with retreat 1 and retreat 2 plus bypassing it, having too high retreat chance would be broken as well and inefficient as a promotion tree maybe
-- for simplicity most unit upgrades are fairly straightforward and relaxed, for example all mounted units can upgrade to the next mounted tier without much restriction, for example chariots upgrade to horse_archers now not to knights anymore, war elephants upgrade to knights not to cuirassiers anymore, a horse archer can become a camel knight or a horse knight, and a camel archer can become a horse knight or a camel knight as well. I assume that the riders themselves can transition to another mount type so it would make sense to reinvest their skills in new mounts hence them being upgradeable. In particular, longbows and crossbows, as well as macemen, and pikemen, now upgrade to musketmen not to riflemen anymore, which makes a lot of sense and is historically more accurate, as well as a lot more balanced as cuirassiers and such other gun units can't abuse these early ranged or melee units that would have no problem and be just as suited if not more to have a gun as well, should help mostly AIs as they tend to build many longbowmen and macemen and such but perhaps also human players depending on strategy. Cuirassiers are a bit stronger (even though quite a bit more expensive too) to compensate and rebalance them. Also note that as of now for similar reasons, dragoon units have been reworked, and now in particular upgrade to tanks. There are also other unit upgrade and such related changes to other units as of now too, see sevopedia ingame or/and tech tree view or/and xml for accurate/updated value(s)
-- similarly, also changed/reworked upgrade paths for naval units if i may say, and while doing so in particular found the very inconsistent or/and nonsensical ironclad not being able to "walk" on ocean tiles??????? Wtf.. So disabled this and now ironclad can "walk" on ocean tiles as all naval units of its era or around it, i didn't check if accurate but would be surprised if not, buffed ironclad too so it is now an upgrade to frigates for example, see [README.md#military-tree-and-changes](/README.md#military-tree-and-changes) for details or/and for all upgrade changes, or/and sevopedia entries of the units or/and related sevopedia entries, or/and xml or docs in advciv-sas mod folder hopefully more balanced this way and making sense.
